cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the AidPage typology (도감) or its data, please cite it as below. 이 유형화·데이터를 쓰시면 아래와 같이 인용해 주세요."
type: dataset
title: "AidPage Atlas — rule-based, rank-free multi-lens profiles of Korean municipalities (v1.7) with national disaster-assistance thresholds, recorded outcomes and evacuation access"
version: "dex-v1.7"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
authors:
  - given-names: Jihwan
    family-names: Oh
    alias: 5-Jihwan
repository-code: "https://github.com/5-Jihwan/aidpage"
url: "https://5-jihwan.github.io/aidpage/atlas.html"
abstract: >-
  Rule-based typology of 256 Korean municipal units (si/gun/gu) across natural hazards
  (flood history, landslide/slope, coastal contact, drought zones), a social hazard
  (traffic), unordered vulnerability traits, and institutional (ordinance) holdings.
  Thresholds are national top-quartile cut-offs within the same unit class; no composite
  score or ranking is produced. v1.4 adds the national recovery-aid threshold layer
  (fiscal-capacity bands under Regulation art. 5①, in force from 2024-11-19) and recorded
  outcomes from the Disaster Yearbook 2012–2024 (central subsidy events, special disaster
  area declarations, severe-damage events). v1.4.1 (2026-09-17) restores Jeongeup-si (52180), which was missing from v1.4 (255 units); merged-unit specification is now 230. Sensitivity specifications (p70/p80 thresholds,
  230-unit aggregation) are shipped alongside for review. v1.5 (2026-10-11) adds an evacuation-access
  layer (share of residents whose shortest walking path to designated temporary housing crosses a
  deep (≥0.5 m) past-flood record, and share more than 60 minutes away at 48 m/min, computed on the
  OSM path network per H3 cell and population-weighted), a 227-unit reporting specification
  (230 minus Sejong and Jeju's two administrative cities), and fills facility gaps in districts
  created by the 2026-07-01 reorganisation. Types are unchanged from v1.4.1.
 v1.7 (2026-10-14) adds a reference line under every indicator bar citing the statute, agency definition or national value it rests on (only two indicators have official thresholds applicable to municipal values: ageing stages 7/14/20% and the MOIS foreign-resident concentration rule), a same-type peer list, an 'all three nearest shelters' evacuation line, unifies the all-records evacuation share with the deep-record rule, restores Jeongeup's traffic value (types v1.4.2) and corrects two labels (registered disability; basic livelihood eligibility). Data are provided on request with a data-use agreement.
keywords:
  - disaster risk
  - Korea
  - municipal typology
  - administrative burden
  - fiscal capacity
  - regression discontinuity
